  "notes": "The Zaytoven bench, and it is the one entry on this axis with genuinely functional harmony. The research: \"harmonic-minor and natural-minor church-organ voicings; more functional harmony than most trap because of the gospel-keyboard lineage. i–iv–V and i–VI–V appear alongside static minor vamps\" — so `harmonic_minor` outweighs `natural_minor` here, `borrowed.V` is raised to 0.35, and the two functional families carry the top weights, which no other entry in this batch does. \"Arpeggiated right-hand figures over a walking left-hand root\" is the highest `melody.densityPerBar` in the batch [6, 11] against Jeezy's [2, 4] — the two poles of the 2005–2010 Atlanta bench, and the pair the research explicitly contrasts. The hats are \"triplet subdivisions … used continuously\", so `base` is `8T` with `continuous` true and `fillDensity` 0.62. ⚠ **The roll frequency is capped and that is an authoring-band limit, not a reading of the record.** The research says 32nd rolls are used *continuously* in this catalog; `rolls.freqPerBar` tops out at 0.20 in this batch's band, so the hat's actual density is carried by the triplet base and the high `fillDensity` rather than by roll count. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium` — the research rates this high-medium and says \"exact tempi vary widely by release\", which is why the band is 130–150 with the Zaytoven skew as the mode rather than a tight range. INFERRED: every velocity figure, the 0.35 borrowed-V rate, and the `slideProb` that stands in for \"short glides between scale tones\". ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
